2026-08-16T15:19:48Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: Wrong fiscal anchor: You based FY2026Q3 on FY2024Q3 (6.29) and a two‑year compounded growth rate because you claimed “no FY2026Q3 prior‑year figure,” but the proper comparable period is FY2025Q3 diluted EPS (GAAP). Deere reports quarterly, and FY2025Q3 should be available and used as the immediate prior‑year baseline for a Q3 forecast. Using FY2024Q3 introduces an unnecessary two‑year bridge and risks a material misstatement of the figure.
2026-08-16T15:19:57Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: Your step from 45,300 (USDm) in FY2025Q2 to 47,502.2 (USDm) for FY2026Q2 explicitly assumes “comparable +1% + non‑comparable +3.861%” = +4.861% YoY, but that basis is wrong for Home Depot: comparable sales is a like‑for‑like store metric and cannot be simply added as a full‑base percentage alongside a “non‑comparable” percentage to derive total net sales growth. Moreover, a +3.861% non‑comparable contribution is implausible for HD’s Q2 given its essentially flat store count and no 14th‑week effect; absent a cited acquisition closing into the base, this construction overstates the growth and inflates the FY2026Q2 net sales to 47,502.2.
2026-08-16T15:20:16Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: You claim to anchor on company guidance for ADI FY2026Q3, which per your own source is “$3.9 billion, +/- $100 million.” The guidance midpoint is 3,900 USDm, but you used 3,946.22 as the guidance_anchor. That contradicts the cited guidance and inflates your blended result; using the correct 3,900 USDm midpoint would materially lower the forecast.
