2026-08-16T15:20:39Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The P&L tie-out uses “5.33e+04 net finance” in the same units as revenue and operating income (USD millions), i.e., $53,300 million, which is three orders of magnitude too large for ADI and drives the -$90 EPS. Net finance should be on the order of ~$53.3 million; using 53.3 (not 53,300) gives post-tax income ≈1,551.9 (USD m) and EPS ≈ $3.11/share, aligning with the $3.30 ± $0.15 guidance. This is a clear units/scale error on the net finance line.
2026-08-16T15:20:40Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: The source evidence mixes metrics: “[reported] FY2025: $17,311 FY 2025” is the Production & Precision Ag segment’s net sales (USDm), not its operating profit. Deere’s segment operating profit is in the low single‑digit billions for a full year, not $17,311m. Using a sales figure as “reported” evidence for operating profit puts the build-up/seasonal baseline on the wrong basis, so the FY2026Q3 operating profit estimate of 493.547 USDm is derived off the wrong metric.
