2026-08-16T15:20:40Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: You blended inputs on different bases. The “seasonal_trend” input (4.68251) is explicitly Adjusted diluted EPS for FY2025Q2 per your source, while the “build_up” input (4.77983) aligns with HD’s reported GAAP diluted EPS for FY2025Q2 (~$4.78–$4.79). Mixing GAAP and Adjusted figures to forecast an Adjusted EPS yields an apples-to-oranges result, so the 4.76902 figure is on the wrong basis.
2026-08-16T15:21:06Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: The 71.95% “last 4 reported levels” base is computed on the wrong basis: you averaged 69.9, 71.6, 74.1, and 72.2 even though, per your own Q3 source rows, 69.9% and 74.1% are the prior-year comparative figures, not the reported quarter (e.g., FY2020/21 Q3 show 71.6% current vs 69.9% prior; FY2022/23 Q3 show 72.2% current vs 74.1% prior). Mixing current and prior-year columns invalidates the average, so the 72.35% result is built on misclassified inputs.
